- Mono/state: `tests/mono_collapse.rs:183` compares ramping/stationary dual and collapsed output; `:246` checks desymmetrization against never-collapsed execution. Native-bank unavailability returns early, so a skipped case is not execution evidence. Retain restore/corruption (lib 5263), bank rejection (5400), invalid automation (5465), reset (5518), nonfinite recovery (5229), and existing silent-rest/automation tests (4617–5100).
- Existing unchanged foundations: `tests/determinism.rs:33` and `src/corpus.rs` for nonvacuous pinned width identity; `tests/gain_law.rs:110,215` for ceiling and f64 oracle; `tests/conformance.rs` for the production-factory harness; `tests/allocation.rs:144` for render allocation/free counts including automation, reset and hostile input. These do not alone prove absence of locks/syscalls: retain source review of the bounded private change. No new allocator, listening campaign, pin regeneration or benchmark machinery.

This is a bounded shortlist proposal, not an exhaustive audit or a performance finding. Resolve the two lowering unknowns independently only after a later authorized boundary; leave priorities and active #537 WIP unchanged.
